  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Real estate consultancy firm Anarock Property Consultants Ltd has filed draft papers with Sebi to raise Rs 1,000 crore through an initial public offering. The proposed public issue comprises a fresh issue of equity shares of up to Rs 550 crore and an offer for sale of up to Rs 450 crore. Under the offer for sale, promoter selling shareholders Peter Properties Ltd and Khushi Trust, alongside investors including various funds managed by 360 ONE, Om Sai Trust, and Colared Consultants and Traders LLP, will offload shares. The company may consider a pre-IPO placement of up to Rs 110 crore, which would reduce the fresh issue size. Proceeds will fund technology investments, talent augmentation, the DSP Acquisition, and general corporate purposes. ICICI Securities, IIFL Capital Services, and 360 ONE WAM are the book-running lead managers.",
